From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alphi <alphi@starchaser.local>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 10:25:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(core): unset signal on oc2 instead of oc in
 obj_disconnect

obj_disconnect found the connection to remove (oc2, the one after oc in the
list) but released the signal of oc, the previous element. The freed oc2 kept
a weak reference in its signal: a dangling pointer and heap corruption on the
next DSP update. This is a plain upstream bug that the pinned plugdata-pd
(2002d63) still has.

Depended on by: every wire removal on a signal outlet (the bridge's
disconnect and the batch_atomic delete/disconnect phases,
MCPBridge.cpp batch_atomic). Drop this patch only when upstream releases oc2.
---
 src/m_obj.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/m_obj.c b/src/m_obj.c
index ebd23dc..97b9bd7 100644
--- a/src/m_obj.c
+++ b/src/m_obj.c
@@ -774,7 +774,7 @@ doit:
         {
             oc->oc_next = oc2->oc_next;
             if(oc2->oc_signal)  {
-                outconnect_unset_signal(oc);
+                outconnect_unset_signal(oc2);
             }
             freebytes(oc2, sizeof(*oc2));
             goto done;
